     // ---- CHANGE 2 of 4: initializeDecoder — add tunneling setup --------------------
     // After the decoder loop (the tryNumber loop) succeeds, attempt to configure
     // tunneled playback on Fire TV. This is done BEFORE videoDecoder.start().
     //
     // The key difference from standard Moonlight: on tunneled playback we do NOT
     // call releaseOutputBuffer(index, renderTimestampNs) for timing — instead we
     // set the presentation timestamp in queueInputBuffer and let the hardware
     // handle it. This eliminates a full Choreographer round-trip per frame.

